## Why This Is Asked

Industrial edge deployment requires balancing privacy preservation with strict latency constraints. This design evaluates multi-stream fusion capabilities, on-device inference optimization, federated learning with differential privacy, and robust drift handling mechanisms.

## Key Concepts

- Privacy-preserving federated learning with DP-SGD
- On-device multi-stream architectures with early exits
- Model compression techniques: quantization and pruning
- Latency and energy budgeting on edge GPUs
- Drift detection and rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Platform-specific implementation for on-device inference
class VideoAnomalyDetector {
  constructor(modelPath) {
    this.model = this.loadQuantizedModel(modelPath);
    this.frameBuffer = new CircularBuffer(30); // 1 second at 30fps
    this.driftDetector = new StatisticalDriftDetector();
  }

  async processFrame(rgbFrame, opticalFlow) {
    const rgbFeatures = await this.model.rgbBranch(rgbFrame);
    const motionFeatures = await this.model.motionBranch(opticalFlow);

    // Early exit after block 2 for latency guarantee
    if (this.confidenceAboveThreshold(rgbFeatures, motionFeatures)) {
      return this.classifier.fusedInference(rgbFeatures, motionFeatures);
    }

    // Full inference for uncertain cases
    return this.model.fullInference(rgbFrame, opticalFlow);
  }

  // Federated learning with differential privacy
  async federatedUpdate(localGradients, dpParams) {
    const noisyGradients = this.addDPNoise(localGradients, dpParams);
    return this.secureAggregation(noisyGradients);
  }
}

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical, CPU-friendly baseline skills for streaming ML with mixed data types (tabular and text) and delayed labels. It evaluates understanding of online learning, feature engineering for text, calibration, and drift handling in production systems.

## Key Concepts

- Multimodal features (numeric telemetry + text diagnostic logs)
- Online learning via partial_fit for streaming updates
- Feature hashing (hashing trick) for text data
- Drift detection using KL divergence
- Probability calibration for reliable confidence scores
- Ensemble methods for combining model streams

## Code Example

```javascript
class BaselineModel {
  constructor() {
    this.scaler = new StandardScaler();
    this.numericModel = new LogisticRegression();
    this.textModel = new LogisticRegression();
  }

  partialFitNumeric(X, y) {
    const Xscaled = this.scaler.partialFit(X);
    this.numericModel.partialFit(Xscaled, y);
  }

  partialFitText(textData, y) {
    const Xhashed = this.hashText(textData);
    this.textModel.partialFit(Xhashed, y);
  }

  predict(probaNumeric, probaText) {
    return (probaNumeric + probaText) / 2;
  }
}
```

